To update the server (make sure you are running as root):
1. Copy the latest client*.zip and Server*.zip into /root/update
2. updateserver

Check the j.err file to make sure there weren't any reported errors.

--------------------------------------------------------------------

Notes:

1. Two files are creates in the directory where you run updateserver:
	+ j.err is the stderr output
	+ j.out is the stdout output
   Please note, this output does not come to the screen -- it just gets written
   into these files. (If you are in /root/update when you run updateserver
   these files will be deleted and you must look at their archived copies in /root/jodie/update-* (see #4 plus date format note below).
2. The updateserver alias runs /root/jodie/updateserver.sh
3. Archives are made using the current date for:
	+ /lle/dist/tomcat/lib/cp4laplink.jar
	+ /lle/dist/tomcat/lib/c4psecurity.jar
	+ /lle/system/portal
4. The zip files and j.err and j.out are archived (using the current date) to /root/jodie/update-*

Date format note
In order that multiple updates may be made in the same day, the date format is MMddyy-S (where S if the number of seconds since epoch).

Example archives:
+ /root/jodie/update.060908-1213041515   -- zip files, j.out and j.err
+ /lle/system/portal.060908-1213041515   -- previous portal tree
+ /lle/dist/tomcat/lib/c4psecurity.jar.060908-1213041515
+ /lle/dist/tomcat/lib/c4plaplink.jar.060908-1213041515

Also note that the c4p.jar file that is remade is found in /lle/system/portal/WEB-INF/lib/jtemp renamed in the same archive format: e.g., c4p.jar.060908-1213041515
